const schema = JSON.stringify({ '@context':'https://schema.org', '@type':'CollectionPage', name:'Mechanics lien state guides and tools', url:'https://mechanicslienform.com/mechanics-lien/', mainEntity:{ '@type':'ItemList', itemListElement:statePages.map((s,i) => ({ '@type':'ListItem', position:i+1, name:s.name, url:'https://mechanicslienform.com/mechanics-lien/'+s.slug+'/' })) } });
---
<StatePage title="Mechanics Lien State Guides & Available PDF Tools" description="Compare twelve state mechanics lien guides. Find notice, recording, and enforcement rules, plus paid PDF preparation tools for seven supported states." canonical="https://mechanicslienform.com/mechanics-lien/" schema={schema}>
 <article class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-12 sm:px-6 prose prose-lg max-w-none"><nav aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> › State guides</nav><h1>Mechanics lien state guides and preparation tools</h1>
 <p>Choose the state where the improved property is located. A contractor's business address does not determine the property's lien procedure. These twelve guides explain different notice, filing, and enforcement workflows; the available paid generators are identified separately below.</p>
 <h2>Find the guide for your property</h2><StateDirectory />
 <h2>Compare the task, office, and clock</h2><p>Start with the contracting role and property type, then identify the event that starts each period. Many states measure a deadline from last furnishing, but Arizona and California require project-completion analysis. Illinois uses four months for third-party protection, and New York distinguishes four- and eight-month filing periods. North Carolina files real-property claims with the clerk of superior court.</p>
 <p>Read the state page before applying a date calculator. Separate early notices from recording, owner service, proof filing, and enforcement. A ten-day notice of intent in Colorado needs lead time before filing; Florida's early Notice to Owner starts with first furnishing. Neither should be postponed until the end of an unpaid job.</p>
 <h2 id="paid-tools">Paid preparation tools — $24.99 per purchase</h2><p>Mechanics lien tools are available for the following seven property states. Each workflow offers a preview before checkout. Filing, legal review, recording fees, postage, and service are separate responsibilities.</p><ul>{statePages.filter(s => s.generator).map(s => <li><a href={'/mechanics-lien/'+s.slug+'/#generator'}>{s.name} mechanics lien preparation tool</a></li>)}</ul>
 <p>For early Florida notices, use the <a href="/notice-to-owner/florida/#generator">Florida Notice to Owner tool</a>. It prepares a notice, not a recorded Florida claim of lien. Illinois, New York, North Carolina, Colorado, and Florida lien guides do not currently offer state-specific mechanics lien generators. Do not select another state's generator for those properties.</p>
 <h2>Build a complete claim file</h2><p>The <a href="/mechanics-lien/form/">form checklist</a> helps gather project records. Match the owner and contracting parties, obtain the property description, reconcile payments and credits, and document the relevant furnishing dates. Keep notice copies and service evidence beside the contract so they can be reviewed together.</p>
 <p>If payment arrives, choose the correct follow-through document. A conditional waiver addresses payment-related rights; a release or discharge identifies an already filed claim. Reserve disputed items carefully and keep proof of cleared funds.</p>
 <h2>Related notice, payment, and release guides</h2><ul>{documentPages.map(p => <li><a href={p.path}>{p.name}</a></li>)}</ul>
 <p>Public projects, bonds, bankruptcy, and missed notices need separate analysis. These guides cover general private-property rules and link to official sources; consult qualified local counsel for a specific claim.</p></article>
</StatePage>